meta {
  name: Delete Triage Record
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

delete {
  url: {{CRM_URL}}/rpa_integrationinboundqueues({{triageRecordId}})
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

script:pre-request {
  const id = bru.getEnvVar("triageRecordId");
  if (!id) {
    throw new Error('triageRecordId is not set. Run "Find Triage Records by Correlation Id" and set it deliberately before deleting.');
  }
  console.log(`about to delete triage record ${id}`);
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Removes one triage record by its primary key. For clearing up records a QA
  run created, not for anything else.

  *Agree deletion with DDTS CRM before running it in a shared organisation.*
  Triage records are the CRM operations team's work queue. A record that
  looks like test noise from this side may be one they are mid-way through
  investigating, and nothing in the entity distinguishes the two.

  It deletes whatever {{triageRecordId}} currently holds, and that variable
  is set as a side effect by both "List Recent Triage Records" and "Get
  Triage Record by Derived Id" — so confirm what it points at before
  running. The pre-request script refuses an empty value and prints the id
  it is about to delete.

  Nothing in fcp-sfd-crm ever deletes, closes or updates a triage record.
  Once a record is written it stays as it is, including after the underlying
  data is corrected and the message replays successfully. Clearing them is a
  CRM-side responsibility with no automation behind it, which is worth
  raising separately from any QA run.
}
